{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787178586050707001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"comely-catty-orangutan","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"450db8e491c1552f6434ce2a7cf5fb67f2cac1e582ac58c979fa2d830b99e196","event_uuid":"eb9bcaab-3a98-4d5d-9e52-7c675d2cef2c","position":{"commit_sha":"4f5d2e000db564a84ecebd17d0f10e892f647f1e","position":"1787175851390396001-eb9bcaab-3a98-4d5d-9e52-7c675d2cef2c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787175851390396001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Target\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py` — **790 LOC** on origin/main against the 800-LOC hard cap (10 lines of headroom).\n\nTen lines of headroom.\n\n## How to do it\nRead the file and derive the seam from the CALL GRAPH — do not take any hint above as the answer.\nExtract a cluster of functions that already call each other and that share one concern. The commit\nmessage must NAME the concern boundary you chose and why the call graph supports it.\n\n## Constraints (inherited from the epic — all non-negotiable)\n- Split along LOGICAL CONCERNS / ARCHITECTURAL BOUNDARIES, never mechanically to hit a number.\n- NEVER raise the limit; `.github/module-size-limit.txt` is locked.\n- No resulting file under 100 LOC; target 200-500 LOC each.\n- Leave REAL headroom — landing at 798 recreates the problem (that is how Gerrit 1916 failed).\n- Behaviour-preserving: existing tests for this area must pass UNMODIFIED. If a test must change,\n  the split was not behaviour-preserving — stop and reconsider the seam.\n- Serena `find_referencing_symbols` for references, THEN `grep` for each moved symbol AS A STRING\n  (monkeypatch.setattr / getattr / importlib). Serena returns EMPTY, not an error, for `Any`\n  receivers, so the grep is mandatory.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py` is under the cap with real headroom, and every new file is >= 100 LOC.\n- [ ] The split follows an existing call-graph seam; the commit message names the concern boundary.\n- [ ] Behaviour unchanged: existing tests covering this area pass UNMODIFIED.\n- [ ] The CI module-size gate passes without touching `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; the complexity ratchet shows no new or increased entries.\n- [ ] All references updated — verified by BOTH a semantic reference search AND a string grep.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","9224-5753-c3a9-4c33"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9224-5753-c3a9-4c33","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8c3b-7479-e09d-465b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Split llm/workflow/executor.py (790 LOC) along its concern boundary","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["eb9bcaab-3a98-4d5d-9e52-7c675d2cef2c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787178586050707001,"uuid":"01ab9b49-6b2e-42e3-b4a2-8c895c46348b"}